  "commit_message": "fix(api): close dec.More() blind spot in upload validation\n\nFollow-up on my own 5efb9cc. The Copilot reviewer flagged dec.More() as\nunreliable for detecting trailing top-level data. Its stated examples were\nwrong — More() is implemented as `peek() != ']' && peek() != '}'`, so both\n`{\"a\":1}{\"b\":2}` and `{...} junk` were already rejected, and the existing\ntests prove it. But the underlying concern holds for the one case that\nimplementation cannot see: when the trailing byte *is* `]` or `}`, peek()",
